---
source: misc/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"cal\")"
---
Display a calendar

Usage: cal [OPTIONS] [ARGS]...

Arguments:
  [ARGS]...  Positional arguments: [[[day] month] year]

Options:
  -1, --one                Display single month output (default)
  -3, --three              Display three months spanning the date
  -n, --months <MONTHS>    Display number of months starting from the date
  -s, --sunday             Display Sunday as the first day of the week
  -m, --monday             Display Monday as the first day of the week
  -y, --year               Display a calendar for the whole year
  -Y, --twelve             Display a calendar for the next twelve months
  -j, --julian             Use day-of-year (ordinal) numbering
  -w, --week               Print the week numbers alongside the days
  -c, --columns <COLUMNS>  Number of columns to use (`auto` lets cal pick a value that fits the
                           terminal width) [default: auto]
  -h, --help               Print help
